+### 3.4 Pipeline placement
+
+Ghosts do NOT go into the splat layers (the first cut did, and it was wrong). The splat overlay
+runs inside the DOF stage and adds into `$HDRTarget`, which the glare family thresholds
+afterwards for its light sources — so every ghost above the glare threshold grew its own
+diffraction streaks, anamorphic flare and filter star. Physically a ghost is already a
+second-order internal reflection; a flare struck off one is third order, ~1/50–1/200 of the
+ghost, and invisible. **Ghosts are not light sources.**
+
+So the ghost draws accumulate into a dedicated full-resolution RGBA16F layer
+(`$DofGhostLayer`, allocated only on frames ghosts run, cleared each such frame, dropped on
+resize), and `CDepthOfFieldStage::ExecuteGhostComposite()` — a single full-screen
+`GS_BLSRC_ONE | GS_BLDST_ONE` pass, technique `DofGhostComposite` — adds it into
+`$HDRTarget` from `CStandardGraphicsPipeline::ExecuteHDRPostProcessing`, immediately after
+`CBloomStage::Execute()`. That point is after the half- and quarter-resolution downsamples of
+the HDR target, i.e. after every thresholded source has been extracted (bloom, streaks,
+anamorphic flare, front filter PSF, halation) and after auto exposure has metered, and before
+the tone map, which is the last reader of the target. The call is unconditional, so **bloom off
+changes nothing**: the ghosts appear at the same place in the frame either way. Being past
+motion blur is also correct — a ghost is formed in the glass and follows its source, not the
+geometry behind it — and it stays undepth-masked as before.
+
+Consequences, accepted: ghosts are not halated (halation's source is thresholded earlier), do
+not bloom, and do not drive auto exposure. With the sprite splat off (`r_DepthOfFieldMode 1`)
+the splat overlay pass is now skipped entirely — the ghosts no longer need it. Cost: one
+full-screen additive pass on frames with ghosts, nothing at all when `Amount <= 0.001`.
+
 ## 4. Acceptance
 
 1. Amount 0: no ghost draw, no cost, frame identical.
